    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a10">

                <pb facs="0281" n="209" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg209"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 10 in No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Granville to Mr. Lowell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 17,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 10th instant, requesting to be furnished with the
                    particulars of the charge against Daniel Sweeney or McSweeney, who is stated to
                    be an United States citizen, and who was arrested under the act for the better
                    protection of person and property in Ireland of March 2, 1881, on the 2d
                    instant, and lodged in Dundalk jail.</p>
                <p>In reply, I beg leave to acquaint you that I have referred your application to
                    the proper department of Her Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
